# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your values
ADMIN_USERNAME=admin
ADMIN_PASSWORD=your-secure-password-here
JWT_SECRET=your-random-secret-key-here

# Optional — your Google Analytics 4 Measurement ID (Admin → Data Streams →
# your web stream → Measurement ID, format G-XXXXXXXXXX). Leave unset to skip
# Google Analytics entirely — the site works fine either way.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX

# ── CRITICAL FOR PRODUCTION / HOSTINGER ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# DATA_DIR — absolute path OUTSIDE the repo for all admin content (projects,
# services, settings, research, team, etc.).
#
# WHY: data/*.json files are tracked in git, so every `git pull` during a
# redeploy overwrites them with the last-committed versions — wiping every
# admin edit made since then.  Pointing DATA_DIR at a persistent folder that
# git never touches fixes this permanently.
#
# HOW to set up on Hostinger (do this ONCE, then every redeploy is safe):
#   1. Open Hostinger File Manager and create:
#        /home/your-username/greenbd_data/
#   2. Add this line to your Node.js app's environment variables in
#      Hostinger hPanel → Hosting → Node.js → Environment Variables:
#        DATA_DIR=/home/your-username/greenbd_data
#   3. Redeploy once — the app auto-copies all default data files there on
#      first start. After that, all admin edits go to that folder and survive
#      every future git pull / rebuild.
#
# DATA_DIR=/home/your-username/greenbd_data

# UPLOADS_DIR — same idea for uploaded images, PDFs, and audio files.
# Set this to the SAME parent folder or a subfolder of DATA_DIR.
#
# UPLOADS_DIR=/home/your-username/greenbd_uploads
